1
00:00:33,338 --> 00:00:35,777
the beginning

2
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:39,700
of the song.

3
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:41,677
We'll be

4
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:44,897
right

5
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:49,817
back to

6
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:53,540
the beginning of the song.

7
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:55,350
Yeah, yeah.

8
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:59,540
It's a big trip, but there's a big thing.

9
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,241
There's a big thing that's there.

10
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:07,960
I'm sorry, I'll keep you safe.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,840
Okay, let's go ahead and go.

12
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:16,180
I'm always going to go to the moon.

13
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:03,860
Hey, somebody go buy some more food!

14
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:05,700
Yeah, we've got the money.

15
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,280
Get some more booze while you're at it.

16
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:14,877
When it comes to painting,
I'm in a league of my own.

17
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,254
So, what do you think?

18
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:28,340
It took all the money.

19
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:35,520
How can I face the others now, dummy?

20
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:40,520
All right, guys, it's time to
kick their asses. All of them.

21
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:47,810
That's it.

22
00:02:47,893 --> 00:02:48,723
Show them.

23
00:02:48,806 --> 00:02:50,284
Looks like you lose this round.

24
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,157
Losers get to go pick up more booze.

25
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:54,037
Buy all the food they
have in the shop, too.

26
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:56,355
It's not like we don't have the money.

27
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:03,440
Be right back.

28
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:05,977
And when I am, I'm
going to win every hand.

29
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:06,890
Just you wait.

30
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,740
What was that? What happened?

31
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:36,220
Who the hell are those guys? You jerks!

32
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:37,595
You got a death wish?

33
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,440
I recognize him!

34
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:57,180
It's that pirate!

35
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,800
Straw Hat Luffy!

36
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:14,968
So you came to get your
money back, did you?

37
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:16,100
Bad move.

38
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:17,832
Just take a look around.

39
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,941
Do you really think the four of
you are enough to handle all of us?

40
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,580
But since you're here,

41
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:30,844
we might as well take those big
bounties you've got on your heads

42
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:35,620
He's the captain of that long-nosed
weakling we took care of earlier

43
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:40,722
With that pitiful excuse for a pirate on
his crew, he can't possibly be that strong

44
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:45,920
Let's go, come on, shrimp

45
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:49,180
Now come, go!

46
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:57,044
What do you think you're doing?

47
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,040
Are you punching him?

48
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:03,553
Not even a bombardment for battleship
cannons can put a den in that armor.

49
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:04,640
What a joke.

50
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:11,191
If you're just gonna play around, then
I'll go ahead and end this right now.

51
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,140
And cannon!

52
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:45,200
He punched a hole right through it!

53
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:48,530
Hey!

54
00:05:48,613 --> 00:05:49,443
Hold on!

55
00:05:49,526 --> 00:05:50,657
Wait a second, you guys!

56
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:52,500
Let's talk about this first.

57
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:55,980
Okay, guys.

58
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:58,760
Okay, guys, fire the cannons.

59
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:00,110
Woo-hoo!

60
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:04,620
Now three-sword style.

61
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:06,320
Karasu.

62
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:13,740
Raven hunt.

63
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:28,570
What?!

64
00:06:28,653 --> 00:06:29,483
Impossible!

65
00:06:29,566 --> 00:06:31,059
Those cannonballs are made of iron!

66
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:39,520
The cannon's too!

67
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:40,840
Holy crap!

68
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:43,020
These guys are seriously bad news!

69
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:45,397
Let's get out of here!

70
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,304
Everyone run for the back door!

71
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:57,100
You guys started this fight.

72
00:06:57,360 --> 00:07:00,301
It's kind of pathetic to
run from it like cowards.

73
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:04,020
Party table kick course!

74
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:19,597
We can't make it to the back door!

75
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,760
Windows! Use the windows!

76
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:23,680
Rumble!

77
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,340
More points!

78
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:39,020
A seal colonnade!

79
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:46,510
Wait!

80
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,197
You just want the money back.

81
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:54,751
The 200 million berries the
long-nosed guy had, is that it?

82
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:58,937
I'm sorry to be the one to tell you, but
that pile of money isn't here anymore.

83
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:02,037
Franky, the family boss, took it
all and went on a shopping spree.

84
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,017
And since he's buying
something on the black market,

85
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:07,697
we don't have any idea where he
might be or even how to find him.

86
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:12,197
So no matter how much of a rampage you go
on, that 200 million won't be coming back.

87
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:13,398
So why don't you...

88
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:17,050
DUMBAY!

89
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:18,810
Shut up.

90
00:08:18,893 --> 00:08:20,291
That's enough out of you.

91
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,935
This has nothing to do with the money.

92
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:24,560
Damn straight.

93
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,520
It's too late for that.

94
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:34,182
Not even your bones will
be left when we're done.

95
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:36,277
Not even our bones?!

96
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:38,817
What's the matter with you
acting like a bunch of cowards?

97
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,257
We're the Franky family!

98
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:42,397
We're the ones who do all the
bone-breaking around here!

99
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,310
Got it?

100
00:08:43,393 --> 00:08:44,597
Never forget who you are!

101
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:48,621
Okay, brothers, let's show them
the specialty of the Franky House!

102
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:56,920
Now, fire the Anything Shot Cannon!

103
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:08,740
Here they come! Awesome! Pull it up!

104
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:11,317
Keep firing till there's
nothing left to shoot!

105
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:12,320
C'mon!

106
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,049
There's only four of them!

107
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,780
What was that? Fireworks?

108
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:38,392
Sounds like it's coming from
out toward the Franky house.

109
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:39,450
Them again?

110
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,097
What trouble are they up to this time?

111
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:43,010
I know, right?

112
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:45,400
Hey, quiet, they're gonna hear us.

113
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:51,457
Oh boy, sounds like they're
getting a little carried away.

114
00:09:51,540 --> 00:09:52,834
When those boys party.

115
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:56,201
They really don't show any
restraint, now do they?

116
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:57,620
No big deal.

117
00:09:57,900 --> 00:09:59,637
It's not like they do it all the time.

118
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,700
It's a nice day.

119
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:19,497
Should we go after Franky?

120
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:21,417
Start looking. Where?

121
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:23,777
Oh man.

122
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:26,977
Looks like these idiots really
didn't know where he took the money.

123
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:32,480
And if we do find him, if he spent
it, then there's no getting it back.

124
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:34,290
What now?

125
00:10:34,373 --> 00:10:37,657
Even if we wait around for him, he
may not be back for quite a while.

126
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:40,640
Okay, the first aid treatment is all done.

127
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:44,617
We need to take him back on a stretcher
so I can use some help over here.

128
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:46,917
Hanging around here won't do any good.

129
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,557
Let's head back to the ship for now.

130
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:50,640
We left Nami there all by herself.

131
00:10:50,740 --> 00:10:52,400
And Robin's still missing.

132
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:55,160
The ship's a problem, too.

133
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:56,810
Yeah.

134
00:10:56,893 --> 00:10:57,880
Hey, Luffy!

135
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,500
I've made a decision.

136
00:11:04,020 --> 00:11:04,850
Huh?

137
00:11:05,280 --> 00:11:06,320
About the ship.

138
00:11:15,860 --> 00:11:18,380
It's time to part ways with the Mary.

139
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,740
We'll say goodbye to her here.

140
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:27,560
All right, then.

141
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:29,020
We'll be leaving now.

142
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:33,360
That man is seriously stubborn.

143
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:34,740
It's infuriating.

144
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:37,737
We don't even know if he has it or not,

145
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:40,717
yet they keep sending me out
here, over and over again.

146
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:44,447
I wish those people would put
themselves in my shoes for once.

147
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,040
It's Khalifa.

148
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,640
Well, come in.

149
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:55,220
You must be worn out, sir.

150
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:57,620
Would you like something to drink?

151
00:11:57,920 --> 00:11:59,360
I would, thank you.

152
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,340
Maybe some tea.

153
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:04,640
I've already prepared it.

154
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:10,200
Well, I'd expect nothing less
from you. Thank you. I'm grateful.

155
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,070
Poor Mr.

156
00:12:14,153 --> 00:12:16,757
Corgi is always so angry
when he leaves, isn't he?

157
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:19,397
What in the world does he
come here to talk about?

158
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,310
Oh, that.

159
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:25,367
Those he represents want something I
have, and they keep making various offers.

160
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:30,473
It must be something of great
importance, then, isn't it?

161
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:34,657
Well, maybe so, though I always
deny knowing anything about it.

162
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:37,700
They really are tiresome people.

163
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:44,250
Hey!

164
00:12:44,333 --> 00:12:47,100
Usopp's finally awake,
you guys! All right!

165
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:48,140
Good to hear!

166
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:51,916
That's one less thing to worry about.

167
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:56,620
Hey, Usopp!

168
00:13:01,860 --> 00:13:03,820
Robin still isn't back yet.

169
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:09,160
You know, I ought to punch
you for scaring us like that.

170
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:11,640
Yeah, no kidding.

171
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:15,197
Though it looks like you've taken
enough punches already, if you ask me.

172
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:18,117
What were you thinking,
taking those guys on alone?

173
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:20,897
You can't just run off and
fight whoever you want.

174
00:13:20,980 --> 00:13:23,215
Oh, that's a good one coming from you.

175
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:27,697
This wouldn't have happened
if I was strong like you guys.

176
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:28,720
I'm sorry.

177
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:30,980
It's all my fault.

178
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,260
I'm so ashamed of myself.

179
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:39,237
I knew how important that money was.

180
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:41,080
Hey, hey, stop. I get it.

181
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:44,457
I know you're sorry, but you don't have
to get all touchy-feely on me, okay?

182
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:49,880
All our savings, all the trouble we went
through, what about the Mary? Take it easy.

183
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,757
You shouldn't be out of bed yet.

184
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:52,958
Come on, calm down.

185
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:55,909
Stop your whining and
listen to the doctor.

186
00:13:57,820 --> 00:14:02,000
So, is there a chance we might
get our money back after all?

187
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:03,677
Well, maybe.

188
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:06,936
We won't know for sure till
that Franky guy shows up.

189
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,120
I see.

190
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,420
I'm sorry.

191
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:11,250
Hey,

192
00:14:11,333 --> 00:14:12,717
even if we can't get the rest back,

193
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:14,917
we still have a hundred
million berries left over.

194
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:15,830
Don't worry.

195
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,840
Yeah, but he lost twice that much.

196
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:22,450
Mommy.

197
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:24,500
Sorry, Usopp.

198
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:26,600
No, it's fine.

199
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:30,757
More importantly, is
Mary going to be okay?

200
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:34,664
I mean, can we get her repaired
with the money that we have left?

201
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:37,877
We're lucky we have all these
awesome shipwrights to work on her,

202
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,997
but I know things are going
to get rough out there?

203
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,497
so I want her to be
stronger than ever before.

204
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:44,462
We aren't having them repair it.

205
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:47,336
We decided to get a new ship instead.

206
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:51,477
I know that we probably should have asked
you first, but we didn't have much choice.

207
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:53,457
Either way, I've made up my mind.

208
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:55,657
The Going Mary has taken good care of us,

209
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:58,975
but it looks like our journey
with her has to end here.

210
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:12,237
Anyway, Ice Pops gave us this
awesome ship catalog to flip through.

211
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,817
There's all kinds of different
ships we could pick from in here.

212
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:17,077
And if we decided to
shop for a used model?

213
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:18,537
We could go bigger than the Mary!

214
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:21,017
and still keep our budget
under $100 million.

215
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:21,930
Wait.

216
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:23,740
Just stop.

217
00:15:24,140 --> 00:15:25,280
I get it, Luffy.

218
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:28,620
But the joke's gone on
long enough, okay? See?

219
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:30,757
Chopper doesn't know you're kidding.

220
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:32,840
Look how upset this is making him.

221
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:37,177
Jeez, Captain, you should know better
than to treat your crew like that.

222
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:39,120
Come on, Nami, back me up here.

223
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:44,470
Hold up.

224
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:48,200
Does that mean we don't
have enough for the repairs?

225
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:51,177
It's because I lost the
$200 million, isn't it?

226
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:53,417
And now we can't afford
the work on the Mary.

227
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,037
Is that what this is about?

228
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:58,337
After all, a first-class shipyard
is going to cost a lot, right?

229
00:15:58,420 --> 00:16:00,097
Would you stop and listen to me?

230
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:04,777
What is it tell me don't
try to sugarcoat it.

231
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:05,720
I'm not okay.

232
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:08,837
I don't even care that you lost
all the money That's over now.

233
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:10,157
That's how you feel then.

234
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:12,477
What's with all this crap
about buying a new ship of you?

235
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:14,501
Stop it fighting isn't gonna help

236
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:17,997
Just calm down for a sec.

237
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,857
I Don't see what I'm doing wrong.

238
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:22,317
He's the one saying all
this dumb stuff I know how

239
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,937
you feel but you shouldn't
get so worked up right now.

240
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:29,177
Listen to Nami Usopp if you don't get
any rest you're not gonna get better!

241
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:31,020
Who cares about me?

242
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:34,477
How can you just sit here when he's
making jokes about getting a new ship?

243
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,217
I'm not joking about anything!

244
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,257
This was a hard decision for me, too!

245
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:40,516
Oh yeah, I feel really sorry for you!

246
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:43,295
Already window shopping for a new toy!

247
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:46,557
You trying to pick a fight with me?

248
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:48,357
I don't want your damn pity, got it?

249
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,817
If you tell me it doesn't
matter that I lost the money,

250
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:53,317
then why are you talking
about buying a new ship?

251
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:54,871
Just spit it out already!

252
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:57,857
If we can't afford the repairs
because I screwed up, then tell me!

253
00:16:57,940 --> 00:17:00,737
Don't show me some stupid
catalog and change the subject!

254
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:02,291
I want to know the truth!

255
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:05,040
The Mary can't be...

256
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:17,250
What?

257
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:19,320
What did you just say?

258
00:17:20,820 --> 00:17:22,880
Don't make me repeat myself.

259
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:25,980
I told you, the Mary
can't be repaired anymore.

260
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:29,077
No matter what we do, we...

261
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:30,900
we can't fix it.

262
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:34,626
Otherwise, I wouldn't
say something like that.

263
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:36,980
You mean this ship?

264
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:39,677
The ship that we're riding
on right now is broken?

265
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:40,590
That's right.

266
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:43,540
It's only a matter of
time before she sinks.

267
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:48,760
What are you talking
about, Luffy? That's nuts.

268
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:49,941
No, I'm serious.

269
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:53,280
The shipwrights took a look
at the Mary themselves.

270
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:56,757
They said she wouldn't even
hold out until the next island.

271
00:17:56,840 --> 00:17:59,260
And it's settled, so that's it?

272
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:01,857
A bunch of strangers
tell you to scrap your

273
00:18:01,940 --> 00:18:03,997
ship and you don't even ask any questions?

274
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:04,910
That's enough!

275
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:10,326
I understand these guys know what they're
talking about, but this is just wrong!

276
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:12,900
Don't give up on the Mary!

277
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:15,757
What about all the adventures
we've gone on together?

278
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:17,997
What about all the battles we've fought?

279
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:19,240
She's our friend!

280
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,797
She's one of us!

281
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:25,080
Are you going to abandon her for
another ship without a second thought?

282
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:33,128
After all we've been through, is that
how little the Mary means to you, Luffy?

283
00:18:36,420 --> 00:18:39,596
I know you're upset, Usopp,
but you need to calm down.

284
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:41,080
Sorry, but no.

285
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:45,820
I'm not pecking down until we settle this.

286
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:47,020
Usopp, please.

287
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:50,650
What?

288
00:18:50,733 --> 00:18:52,873
So you know better than the shipwrights?

289
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:56,397
If we had someone on the crew
who knew about this stuff,

290
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:58,637
we wouldn't have asked
them in the first place!

291
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,820
Then forget them!

292
00:19:00,020 --> 00:19:02,557
We don't need those guys
telling us what to do!

293
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:05,346
I'll repair the Mary
myself, just like before!

294
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:09,017
We've made it this far, so there's
no reason we can't go on that way!

295
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:10,997
Here, I'll get started right now!

296
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:12,668
Come on, guys, help me out!

297
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:14,100
That's not gonna work!

298
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:16,597
That's right, we don't
have enough lumber, do we?

299
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:19,080
I better go buy some at the shipyard.

300
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:21,117
We've got a lot of work to do.

301
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,897
You're not a shipwright, Usopp!

302
00:19:22,980 --> 00:19:23,810
You hear me?

303
00:19:23,893 --> 00:19:24,800
Stop it, Luffy!

304
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:26,570
Yeah, you're right.

305
00:19:26,653 --> 00:19:27,483
I know.

306
00:19:27,566 --> 00:19:28,396
But so what?

307
00:19:28,479 --> 00:19:32,277
I don't see why you're so hung up on
everything those stupid shipwrights say.

308
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:35,677
If they knew what she'd gone through,
they wouldn't give up on the Mary so easy.

309
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:38,020
They just want your money. Usopp?

310
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:39,617
The Mary's our ship,

311
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:43,700
so it's our job to take care of her
without someone else butting in.

312
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:45,720
I'm not giving up.

313
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,637
I won't let them take
the Mary away from me.

314
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:49,760
This is stupid

315
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:54,459
You got fooled by a bunch of salesmen
trying to pawn off a used boat.

316
00:19:54,620 --> 00:19:58,037
Luffy I know wouldn't cave in to some
sales bitch from a total stranger!

317
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:02,277
He'd believe in the strength of the
Mary and the strength of his crew.

318
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:06,637
But here you are acting like you know
everything and ignoring your friends?

319
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:09,537
I can't believe that's the kind
of captain you turned out to be.

320
00:20:09,620 --> 00:20:11,738
I thought you were better than that!

321
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:13,866
You're not being fair, Usopp.

322
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:14,850
Luffy felt the...

323
00:20:14,933 --> 00:20:15,817
You stay out of this!

324
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:16,737
It was my call.

325
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:17,760
I stand by it!

326
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:19,628
There's nothing you can do.

327
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:22,297
We're getting a new ship,
whether you like it or not.

328
00:20:22,380 --> 00:20:24,377
This is the end of the road for the Mary.

329
00:20:24,460 --> 00:20:25,477
I'm not leaving her here.

330
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,977
I don't care what you say.

331
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:29,297
I know you're always trying
to think about the future,

332
00:20:29,380 --> 00:20:31,557
but not everyone on
this crew is like that.

333
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:33,837
I see the Mary as one
of our friends, got it?

334
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:35,997
And I won't abandon her when she's hers.

335
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:37,021
Don't be stupid.

336
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:39,637
Even if she is a friend, that
doesn't mean she's a person.

337
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:42,377
She is to me, and she still
has the strength to live!

338
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:43,757
But you wouldn't appreciate that,

339
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,137
because all you care about is
getting a new ship to play with!

340
00:20:46,220 --> 00:20:47,177
All right, that's enough, both of you.

341
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:49,697
Stop being so selfish and
think about your crew!

342
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:51,237
Dude, listen to yourself!

343
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:54,557
Luffy, don't act like you're the
only one who's torn up about this!

344
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:56,037
We all feel the same way!

345
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:58,717
If that was true, then you
wouldn't be looking for a new ship!

346
00:20:58,800 --> 00:20:59,630
All right, fine!

347
00:20:59,713 --> 00:21:01,577
If you don't like the way
your captain does things,

348
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:04,072
then why don't you go ahead and get on...

349
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:08,570
Sanji!

350
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:16,060
This is going way too far.

351
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:18,642
What the hell is wrong with you?

352
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:20,217
If you don't watch it,

353
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:24,065
you're going to say something you
can't take back, so calm down!

354
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:31,580
Yeah, I'm sorry.

355
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:33,817
I don't know what I was thinking.

356
00:21:33,900 --> 00:21:38,217
You don't have to apologize, because
that's how you really feel, isn't it?

357
00:21:38,300 --> 00:21:39,340
That's not true!

358
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:46,632
Just get rid of your dead weight and
move on before they can slow you down.

359
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:52,895
If you're going to throw away the
Mary, might as well throw me away too.

360
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:56,867
I know you're pissed off, but
don't say stupid crap like that.

361
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:58,220
No, I'm serious.

362
00:21:58,620 --> 00:22:01,326
I've been thinking about
this for a while now.

363
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:04,317
It isn't like it was before.

364
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:06,337
You guys are just too strong for me.

365
00:22:06,420 --> 00:22:07,920
I can't keep up anymore.

366
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,800
I mean look what happened today.

367
00:22:11,040 --> 00:22:13,334
You can't even trust me with your money

368
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:18,106
No point in keeping me around if
all I do is cause you trouble?

369
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:25,864
You don't want weak people
on your crew, do you?

370
00:22:27,240 --> 00:22:31,122
Luffy, I still believe that you'll
be King of the Pirates one day.

371
00:22:31,560 --> 00:22:34,060
But as for me, I'm just lucky.

372
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:35,985
I was able to make it this far

373
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:39,977
Even back when we first met
and I was gonna set off alone.

374
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:43,360
You probably just invited
me on your ship out of pity.

375
00:22:44,040 --> 00:22:45,628
What are you talking about?

376
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:46,640
Get on already.

377
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:48,037
We're friends, right?

378
00:22:48,120 --> 00:22:48,950
So get on!

379
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:55,002
That's the only reason I'm here.

380
00:22:57,240 --> 00:23:01,475
There's no sense traveling together
if we don't even have the same goal!

381
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:05,402
Hey, Usopp, where are you going?

382
00:23:06,420 --> 00:23:09,140
Wherever I go, it's my business.

383
00:23:09,580 --> 00:23:11,815
It has nothing to do with you anymore.

384
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:14,640
Sorry, guys.

385
00:23:18,080 --> 00:23:19,420
I'm leaving the crew.

386
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:20,880
This is goodbye.

387
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:42,230
Fine.

388
00:23:42,460 --> 00:23:43,840
Have it your way, then.

389
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:48,270
Uthab!

390
00:23:49,620 --> 00:23:51,000
Get back here!

391
00:23:51,220 --> 00:23:55,980
It shouldn't be like this! Come
on! We can talk! Yeah! Come back!

392
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:57,820
I want you to stay!

393
00:23:58,260 --> 00:23:59,680
Don't leave us!

394
00:24:02,900 --> 00:24:04,120
Uthab, please!

395
00:24:05,900 --> 00:24:06,840
Say something.

396
00:24:16,940 --> 00:24:19,600
Luffy, I'm sorry I can't
follow you anymore.

397
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:24,165
And I'm sorry I was a
pain till the bitter end.

398
00:24:26,440 --> 00:24:30,381
I know you're the captain of this
ship, so the Mary belongs to you.

399
00:24:32,620 --> 00:24:35,800
That's why I want you to
fight me, Monkey D. Luffy.

400
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:46,260
I challenge you to a duel!

401
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:54,750
Huh?

402
00:24:54,833 --> 00:24:56,820
Whoa, wait, what are you saying?

403
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:04,180
At 10 o 'clock tonight, I'll be back, so
you better be ready for a fight, Captain.

404
00:25:04,780 --> 00:25:07,177
I can't stop you from
destroying your own ship,

405
00:25:07,260 --> 00:25:09,966
but if I win, I'm taking
the Mary and leaving.

406
00:25:10,760 --> 00:25:14,819
Either way, when we're done, the
last bond between us will be broken.
